      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of primary leptomenigeal lymphoma (PLML) in an 11-year-old boy presenting with headache, vomiting, and diplopia. The patient was treated on an advanced non-Hodgkin lymphoma protocol with systemic/intrathecal chemotherapy without cranial radiotherapy. He remains in complete remission 33 months after treatment."},
